Herein lies some major spoilers, so be forewarned.

Don't say I didn't warn you.

A few of us here have recently discovered that a single fully charged wand of
wishing (henceforth WoW) can yield an unbounded number of wishes (with some
work but with _no other objects_).  Here's the recipe:

Use the wand's wishes as follows:

	wish 1: 2 blessed scrolls of charging
	wish 2: a blessed wand of polymorph
	wish 3: 3 blessed scrolls of scare monster
	(now use the/a blessed scroll of charging on the WoW)
	wish 4: 3 cursed scrolls of genocide
	wish 5: 3 cursed scrolls of genocide
	wish 6: 3 cursed scrolls of genocide
	wish 7 (after much zapping): 3 cursed scrolls of genocide

Now find a small room and lock all the doors.  Drop the/a scroll of scare
monster, and use the cursed scrolls of genocide one at a time to genocide
minotaurs.  Lo and behold, each one creates 4-6 minotaurs.  Kill them at your
leisure, safely standing on the scroll of scare monster.

When the slaughter is done, pile up all of those wands of digging and start
polymorphing them.  Since you got ~6 scrolls of genocide, and each one produces
~5 minotaurs, you should have ~30 wands of digging.  By the time your wand of
polymorph (and the other scroll of charging you may have gotten) runs out, you
should have produced another WoW or another wand of polymorph.  Repeat the
minotaur process with the first few WoWs you produce, until you have a huge
pile of wands.  At that point polymorphing the pile produces WoWs at a
comfortable rate.

There are a few small ways in which this technique can be improved, but there
are enough spoilers here as it is.

In light of this discovery, I think that the game should be changed to prevent
"breeding" WoWs.  I have two suggestions for how this could be implemented.
The simplest would be to prevent polymorphed wands from becoming WoWs.  This
would probably make the game too difficult to win.  A compromise solution would
be to reduce the probability of getting one every time one is made, effectively
limiting the number a player could get to about 10.  Anybody who can't win the
game after 60 wishes isn't playing right :-).

